// prefix_connected_fine_chain.vo.expected: expected VO derived by hand from doc/formal (ir_vo.tex WF-VO-*,
// passes.tex I1-I5 and the planner O-/S-/R- rules), independently of the producer.
// Every step is preceded by the rule that fixes its position; RULE GAP marks a position the rules leave open,
// with the tie-break used.
// Planner prefix connected,fine.
// c0=Edge(a,b), c1=Edge(b,c), c2=Edge(d,c)
// RULE GAP (O-Fine): "first eligible remaining variable" and "first holding atom" are not ordered by any rule.
// Derivation reads the variable sequence as the heuristic order of first introduction and "first holding atom"
// as the least holding atom under the planner rank at the current B; written position last (I4).
// Variable sequence: a, b, c, d.
struct OrientedChain ; relation Edge (src : i32 [0] , dst : i32 [0]) ; answer (a , d) : - Edge (a , b) , Edge (b , c) , Edge (d , c) ;
valuation {
    // fineStep(a): only holder c0
    Edge @ 0 (a , _) ;
    // fineStep(b): holder c0 (connected) before c1 (disconnected)
    Edge @ 0 (a , b) ;
    // introduce(b): check of other holder c1
    Edge @ 1 (b , _) ;
    // fineStep(c): c1 connected, c2 disconnected -> c1
    Edge @ 1 (b , c) ;
    // introduce(c): check of other holder c2
    Edge @ 2 (_ , c) ;
    // fineStep(d): only holder c2; full row
    Edge @ 2 (d , c) ;
}
